From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:53:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: give the aggregator TNOC its
 peripheral ID

The AMBA bus reads a primecell's peripheral and component IDs from the
end of its register window. For the aggregator Trace NOC at 0x111b8000
that read does not return a CoreSight component ID, so amba_match()
defers the device on every AMBA driver registration and the boot log
ends with "amba 111b8000.tn: deferred probe pending: (reason unknown)".

The vendor device tree of the OnePlus Pad 4 does not read the ID from
the hardware either: it sets arm,primecell-periphid = <0xf0c00>, the
first ID of the TNOC driver's table. Do the same, so the bus matches
the device without touching the hardware.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index e37e59f88bdf..f188ba29c392 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -6749,6 +6749,8 @@
 		tn@111b8000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,coresight-tnoc", "arm,primecell";
 			reg = <0x0 0x111b8000 0x0 0x4200>;
+			/* the ID registers cannot be read at the end of this window */
+			arm,primecell-periphid = <0x000f0c00>;
 
 			clocks = <&aoss_qmp>;
 			clock-names = "apb_pclk";
